      "source": [
        "### Q1. CNN, RNN/LSTM and GAN Concept Matching (Marks: 5)\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Concept Matching Table\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | Suitable Data | Cyber-Security Example |\n",
        "| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
        "| **CNN** | Images / grid-like data | Malware image classification or packet-payload matrix visualization |\n",
        "| **RNN / LSTM** | Sequences / logs / time series | Sequential intrusion detection or network traffic authentication-log analysis |\n",
        "| **GAN** | Synthetic-data generation | Generating controlled synthetic cyber-attack samples for data augmentation |\n",
        "| **Dense Network** | Small numeric feature table | Normal / Attack binary classification based on activity metrics (as done in this lab) |\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Why is a Dense Network used in the practical implementation of this lab?\n",
        "A dense network is used because the input dataset (`simple_cyber_activity.csv`) consists of a small set of structured, independent numerical features (`failed_logins`, `login_hour`, `new_device`, and `data_transfer_mb`). There is no inherent spatial grid-like structure (which would require a CNN) or sequence/temporal dependencies (which would require an RNN/LSTM) in these independent tabular attributes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Q2. Dataset Preparation, Split and Normalization (Marks: 5)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ob9OZDa-fEts"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load dataset\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv('simple_cyber_activity.csv')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Select features\n",
        "features = [\n",
        "    'failed_logins',\n",
        "    'login_hour',\n",
        "    'new_device',\n",
        "    'data_transfer_mb'\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define input (X) and output (y)\n",
        "X = df[features]\n",
        "y = df['label']\n",
        "\n",
        "# Split dataset into training and testing sets\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    test_size=0.25,\n",
        "    random_state=42,\n",
        "    stratify=y\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply feature scaling\n",
        "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
        "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display dataset shapes\n",
        "print('Training shape:', X_train_scaled.shape)\n",
        "print('Testing shape:', X_test_scaled.shape)"
      ],
